  "scope": [
    "Ports display-only Mario Kart Pad identity; Wii scraper/gameID/save/launch routing retained",
    "Dolphin phone-shake binding/runtime queue; existing core and original JIT helper sources retained",
    "Dolphin HD texture region confirmation, common prefix support and atomic import; filenames retained",
    "NeoSwap file-backed fallback with quota-only configuration, per-allocation mappings and distinct actual host/client telemetry",
    "Experimental NONVOLATILE Mach shared pages from up to eight authenticated process sessions of one donor bundle; verified chunk handles/ledger accounting and bounded loans",
    "Eleven audited RPCS3 postimages including coherent host-visible Vulkan SYSTEM buffer imports for selective v0.10.1 fixes and optional client diagnostics; historical JIT/VM/GoW3/save contracts retained",
    "Exact candidate workflow gates, private encrypted packaging and separate macOS 8GiB stress success/refusal evidence; no physical iPhone or 8GiB RAM result claimed",
    "Dusklight v2.0.3 with four reviewed canonical upstream merges; ABI v7, SDL, disc routing and unrelated native cores retained; KartPad 0.7.2 requires a separate game-pack migration",
    "Build 368 device journal analysis; compression-category deltas preserve measured totals and reject true excess; donor errors clear only after current-session authenticated pool adoption, verification and acknowledgements; real-device 1GiB gameplay remains unvalidated",
    "Requested Dolphin/ARMSX2 bulk import: ordinary eight-letter TXT titles and explicit PNACH groups containing comments; damaged code and empty-group rejection retained; no GCT titles invented",
    "KartPad v0.7.3 migration input pins and read-only personal-pack ABI/fingerprint inspection; installed Core remains v0.5.1 until compatible personal input and lifecycle migration",
    "Separate macOS NSXPC 1GiB/Metal feasibility experiment only; no production GPU path, dummy allocation, Core source or physical iPhone/RPCS3 gameplay proof",
    "Build371: canonical coherent Vulkan SYSTEM buffer imports with capability/type/alignment checks, renderer memory budgets and deferred buffer/memory/loan retirement; exact-source macOS MoltenVK 1.4.2 GPU proof required before IPA packaging; actual iPhone gameplay remains unvalidated",
    "Build372: MIT Guest Page Relay adaptation with authenticated named-memory transport and observed creator exit, 8GiB requested capacity from sixteen 512MiB named objects, shared backing tokens and coherent aliases, bounded cleanup, pressure handling and normal allocation fallback; separate relay ABI v1 and fifth embedded extension; RPCS3 guest data integrated explicitly while native executable JIT pages and other emulator cores remain unchanged; capacity is never reported as resident RAM and physical-iPhone/gameplay remains unvalidated",
    "Build373: reviewed iPhone SDK public native-width vm_* APIs and explicit Mach right cleanup; unchanged relay capacity/lifetime/fallback and all Core inputs; improved real-kernel residency observability with the original 1GiB/1MiB tolerance unchanged; independent mandatory Simulator proof, exact candidate hash lock, new private encryption recipient and correctly numbered test package; no physical-iPhone or gameplay validation claim",
    "Build374: donor growth watchdog distinguishes an in-progress authenticated chunk proof from an idle heartbeat; 8GiB stress keeps the existing per-chunk verification and 60s chunk deadline instead of aborting after six seconds during high-memory verification; Core inputs, relay ABI, quotas and fallback remain unchanged; physical-iPhone/gameplay validation remains pending",
    "Build375: canonical 1GiB Vulkan provenance keeps every unchanged donor/runtime source pinned to abc9566 and separately pins the exact reviewed Build374 NeoSwapDonorIPC watchdog SHA-256 plus candidate manifest identity; no Vulkan, allocator, relay, Core or gameplay behavior is relaxed",
    "Build376: relay CI artifacts replace the prior same-name artifact on workflow reruns so IPA evidence always consumes the successful current attempt; source identity, Simulator behavior, relay capacity, donor runtime, Vulkan path and Core inputs remain unchanged",
    "Build378: delivery-only correction; the validated NeoStation IPA is copied unchanged into the private Actions artifact as NeoStation.ipa, the artifact guard requires exactly one raw IPA, and the same SHA-256, validations, runtime, cores and no-public-release policy are preserved",
    "Build379: fix the on-device NeoSwap hookup observed in Build378: RPCS3 waits up to 10s for the retained 8GiB guest relay and refuses Core initialization instead of silently committing guest shared memory to file fallback; donor helpers prewarm a measured 1GiB backing floor in bounded 128MiB chunks subject to real system headroom/pressure, then grow further on actual RPCS3 demand; game-time diagnostics expose relay live/object/alias bytes; no virtual capacity is relabeled as resident RAM",
    "Build380: preserve the Build379 RPCS3 relay and measured 1GiB donor-floor runtime unchanged; make all donation evidence uploads replace same-name artifacts on workflow reruns so IPA packaging cannot consume stale failed Simulator/stress reports; direct raw IPA delivery remains enabled",
    "Build380 manifest correction: recompute the NeoSwap IPA workflow SHA-256 over UTF-8 bytes so the explicit candidate hash lock matches the workflow containing the bullet character; runtime and delivery behavior are unchanged",
    "Build381: grow measured NeoSwap donor backing toward a 5GiB aggregate goal using up to two independent helper processes in parallel, normally 512MiB chunks with an automatic 256MiB fallback after a large-chunk refusal; production donor chunk ceiling is raised to 512MiB and chunk verification timeout to 60s while kernel/system headroom checks, measured resident/compressed accounting and cleanup remain fail-closed",
    "Build381: simplify the RPCS3 performance overlay to FPS plus a 60-second memory comparison graph: measured NeoSwap donor memory (resident + accounted compressed pages) versus the NeoStation/RPCS3 iPhone process phys_footprint; 5GiB is a donor target, not a claim of simultaneous physical residency",
    "Build381 follow-up: the legacy 12-locale NeoSwap status catalogue remains validated for compatibility while the simplified performance overlay intentionally stops rendering the old verbose swap-status paragraph; tests now reject unknown reintroduced keys and require the NeoSwap/iPhone-RAM graph contract",
    "Build381 provenance follow-up: the canonical 1GiB Vulkan proof keeps all unchanged donation/Vulkan runtime files pinned to abc9566 and separately pins the exact reviewed Build381 NeoSwapDonorIPC and NeoSwapDonorRequestHandler SHA-256 values for the 512MiB growth ceiling; reruns overwrite same-name evidence artifacts",
    "Build382: preserve the Build381 5GiB/512MiB/256MiB runtime and FPS/NeoSwap/iPhone-RAM overlay unchanged; make stress evidence accept a fully verified 8GiB resident+compressed ledger without falsely claiming simultaneous 8GiB residency, and extend only the hosted iOS18 Simulator launch-evidence deadline to survive slow first-boot data migration",
    "Build383: preserve the Build381 5GiB donor/runtime policy and Build382 evidence semantics; extend only the macOS stress-probe session/chunk deadline for late high-capacity verification, and resize the native RPCS3 performance overlay to 320x250 so the FPS graph and NeoSwap-versus-iPhone-RAM graph are fully visible",
    "Build384: preserve the Build381/383 5GiB runtime, 512/256MiB two-helper growth and FPS/NeoSwap/iPhone-RAM overlay; fix only the iOS18 Simulator proof harness so its private NeoSwapPlugin category and manually seeded state use donorPendingIndexes, donorPendingMaximums and donorFallbackUntil instead of the removed single donorPendingIndex property",
    "Build385: replace eager 5GiB donor warmup with a session-scoped adaptive RPCS3 pool: 512MiB warm floor, 512MiB reserve, 128MiB growth quantization and a 5GiB hard limit; grow only with actual routed demand, pause growth under measured system pressure, retain prepared pages while the session is active, retire after all loans are released, and display active RPCS3 donor loans against the currently prepared pool"
  ],
